{"name":"Hello Fall","hex":"#995533","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"hello","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Interjection","definitions":["A greeting (salutation) said when meeting someone or acknowledging someone’s arrival or presence.","A greeting used when answering the telephone."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["\"Hello!\" or an equivalent greeting."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hello"},{"term":"fall","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To be moved downwards.\nTo move to a lower position under the effect of gravity.","To move to a lower position under the effect of gravity."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The act of moving to a lower position under the effect of gravity.","A reduction in quantity, pitch, etc."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fall"}],"entries":[{"title":"Hello","blocks":[{"text":"Hello is a salutation or greeting in the English language. It is first attested in writing from 1826."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b3/TelephoneHelloNellie.jpg/330px-TelephoneHelloNellie.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hello","wikidata":"Q98815142"},{"title":"Autumn","blocks":[{"text":"Autumn, also known as fall in North American English, is one of the four temperate seasons on Earth. Outside the tropics, autumn marks the transition from summer to winter, beginning in September or March. Autumn is the season when the duration of daytime becomes noticeably shorter and the temperature cools considerably. Day length decreases and night length increases as the season progresses until the winter solstice in December and June. One of its main features in temperate climates is the striking change in colour of the leaves of deciduous trees as they prepare to shed."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/D%C3%BClmen%2C_Wildpark_--_2014_--_3808_color_balanced.jpg/330px-D%C3